      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "I believe that in #178, the user was using \"architectures\": [\"BitNetForCausalLM\"] in config.json with a capital 'N', but the architecture is registered as \"architectures\": [\"BitnetForCausalLM\"] with a small 'n' in the script convert-hf-to-gguf-bitnet.py, which was causing the error. I don't think it is better to change the name in the script instead of changing the architecture name in config.json. But I also think everyone will use capital N first, as the repo name is BitNet.",
